    "problem": "For the parametric curve\n$$\n\\displaystyle x = t^{2} + t, y = t^{2} - t,-4 \\le t \\le 4,\n$$\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$t$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$a$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$c$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$b$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFind the value of $a + b + c$.",
    "worked_solution": "Substitute the indicated parameter values: $a=(-2)^2+(-2)=2$, $b=0^2-0=0$, and $c=3^2+3=12$. Thus $a+b+c=14$.",
